description:
## Goal

Render clause-coverage warnings from typed reachable failure evidence so the diagnostic names an actual uncovered input and offers a remedy that matches the construct and the demanded program.

## Correct premise

After fz-kdt.36.1 and fz-kdt.36.2, coverage is not checked against an invented undeclared-any or whole-contract domain. A warning exists only because a demanded function-head or local-dispatch input row can reach Dispatch Fail. The diagnostic must explain that reachable failure.

## Strategy

Extend the authoritative typed dispatch reachability result only as far as needed to retain a deterministic canonical failure witness or failure row. Preserve argument correlation and branch-local refinements; do not reconstruct a witness from syntax, union parameter columns, enumerate type products, or expose raw Ty ids. Store semantic evidence independently from source-version spans and render through the warning-fact provenance projection.

## TDD

Prove:

- a function-head warning names the reachable uncovered argument row and the parameter position/shape that escapes;
- case and with-else warnings name the reachable uncovered subject;
- correlated tuple/list rows remain correlated in the witness;
- guarded fallthrough is explained as a possible guard-false path when appropriate;
- function help uses function-clause syntax and distinguishes fixing the caller/domain from deliberately adding a final clause;
- case/with help uses the correct arm syntax;
- quicksort remains warning-free and receives no invented missing-spec advice;
- witness rendering is canonical across process, FIFO/LIFO, and stress permutation;
- location-only replacement changes only provenance.

## Removal

Delete the generic every-input wording and unconditional wildcard help, obsolete undeclared-domain guidance, witness reconstruction helpers, and old diagnostics goldens. Update diagnostic, pattern-matching, and user-facing guides in the same commit. Full focused, fixture, CLI, formatting, check, and strict-Clippy gates pass.
